    {
      "id": "ML-C92-bhakshanam",
      "sequence": 3250,
      "title": "ഭക്ഷണം (bhakṣaṇaṁ) — food",
      "headword": "ഭക്ഷണം",
      "romanization": "bhakṣaṇaṁ",
      "gloss": "food — the general word this book had no room for while it was naming particular dishes",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:f83b4a4081e3dafc",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the word for a meal. Say the word for cooked rice. Then try to say food and notice that you cannot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഭക്ഷണം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭക്ഷണം — bhakṣaṇaṁ — food."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This book has been unusually specific about eating. You own ഊണ്, a meal; ചോറ്, cooked rice; അരി, the raw grain — and until now no word for the category all of them belong to."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is a common shape in a vocabulary that grows from the particular outward, and it is worth naming when it happens: a language course can leave you able to order lunch and unable to say the word food."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 4,
              "utterances": [
                "അരി, raw rice.",
                "ചോറ്, cooked rice.",
                "ഊണ്, a meal.",
                "ഭക്ഷണം (bhakṣaṇaṁ), food — all of it."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It ends in ം, so you already know how it will behave when anything attaches to it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
